  "decision_conditions": [
    "The installed brick boundary treatment and brick piers, due to its siting, appearance and height would appear visually intrusive and not in-keeping with the open character of the surrounding area, resulting in adverse impact on character and appearance of the existing street scene, contrary to Paragraph 135 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policies D3 of the London Plan 2021, Policy DM10 of the Council's Core Strategy 2012.\r",
    "Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that the installed boundary treatment due to its height, material and siting would accommodate adequate visibility splays and therefore would not have an adverse impact on highway safety contrary to Paragraph 116 of the NPPF, 2024 and Policies DM9 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that raised ground levels in the rear garden would not adversely affect the adjoining property No 35 in terms of increased risk of surface water flooding, as such the proposal is contrary to Policy SI13 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS1 and DM4 of the LDF Core Strategy Adopted (2012).\r\r"
  ],
